vendored: unmodified src/ and include/ only. No common/, ggml/, tools or server.

This sync uses ggml 0.26.0. All public ggml headers match the published
transcribe-cpp-sys 0.4.1 headers byte-for-byte except ggml-backend.h, whose
only difference is transcribe's additive backend registration filter API.
transcribe pins ggml d7cb574130e6f01ad25b3289685489200febcd74 and applies
its downstream patches; llama is compiled against the installed, patched
transcribe headers, never against a separately vendored ggml.

transcribe-cpp-sys 0.4.1 already has links=transcribe and emits include_dir
and lib_dir metadata, so no upstream patch is required. DEP_TRANSCRIBE_INCLUDE_DIR
is used by CMake and bindgen. Its transitive rustc-link-lib directives supply
the static transcribe, ggml, backend and ggml-base archives plus system libraries.
This crate builds only a static llama archive. Static source builds are the
supported posture; shared/dynamic-backends need separate packaging validation.

Run independently of the app's Cargo graph:
  CMAKE_ARGS=-DTRANSCRIBE_VULKAN=OFF cargo run --release -j8 \
    --manifest-path vendor/llama-cpp-sys/Cargo.toml --example s1_cleanup -- \
    /path/to/s1-mini-q4_k_m.gguf /path/to/silero-vad-v6.2-F32.gguf

Enable --features vulkan on Linux/Windows or --features metal on macOS.
These forward exclusively to transcribe-cpp-sys. Initialize transcribe backends
before loading either model; llama sees the same process-global ggml registry.
The example defaults to 99 GPU layers (CPU fallback when no GPU is registered).
Optional positional arguments select thread count and GPU layer count.

S1-mini by Superwhisper is not bundled. Its required LICENSE and NOTICE are
retained under examples/S1-mini-{LICENSE,NOTICE}. The example uses its exact
system prompt, styling controls and Qwen3 non-thinking prefix, greedy decoding,
a 1024-token context and a 512-token output limit. The twelve inputs reproduce
/home/aditya/Projects/.s1-exp/run_cases.py. Silero VAD runs before and after
cleanup with both models resident, checking identical silence probabilities.
